{"uid":"be9c625a9978bb80","name":"test_the_failed_petitioned_tasks_dependents_are_repointed_onto_the_remedy_task","fullName":"tests.test_petitions#test_the_failed_petitioned_tasks_dependents_are_repointed_onto_the_remedy_task","historyId":"9e85938f6dfd8789092d580fb03d25b4","time":{"start":1791980264661,"stop":1791980264664,"duration":3},"description":"Why the `(petition REFUTED for task <id>)` suffix on `evidence` is\n    load-bearing rather than decoration: it is what makes `insert_cure_\n    tasks`' existing whole-word `_failed_task_ids_named_in` scan recognise\n    the task the refutation just failed and hand every one of its dependents\n    to the remedy task. The failed task is never resurrected -- it cannot be,\n    `transitions.TASK_STATUS_TABLE[\"failed\"] == (\"skipped\",)` -- so a\n    replacement task inheriting the dependents is the only sanctioned escape\n    from the doom the `substance` branch creates.\n\n    And it is the ONLY task handed over (#209, unit 8). `insert_cure_tasks`\n    scans a reviewer's finding's `clause` as well as its `evidence` for dead\n    ids, but a synthesized remedy finding's `clause` is the filed OBLIGATION\n    -- for a `contradictory-clauses`/`self-referential` petition, the affected\n    task's own `successCriteria` verbatim, which a planner may write naming\n    other task ids. Scanning it re-pointed the dependents of an unrelated\n    `failed` task onto a remedy task that does not do its work: schedulable\n    again, reporting over work nobody will now do, and with no event to read\n    it off, since only REJECTED edges emit.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Why the <code>(petition REFUTED for task &lt;id&gt;)</code> suffix on <code>evidence</code> is<br />\nload-bearing rather than decoration: it is what makes <code>insert_cure_ tasks</code>' existing whole-word <code>_failed_task_ids_named_in</code> scan recognise<br />\nthe task the refutation just failed and hand every one of its dependents<br />\nto the remedy task. The failed task is never resurrected -- it cannot be,<br />\n<code>transitions.TASK_STATUS_TABLE[&quot;failed&quot;] == (&quot;skipped&quot;,)</code> -- so a<br />\nreplacement task inheriting the dependents is the only sanctioned escape<br />\nfrom the doom the <code>substance</code> branch creates.</p>\n<pre><code>And it is the ONLY task handed over (#209, unit 8). `insert_cure_tasks`\nscans a reviewer's finding's `clause` as well as its `evidence` for dead\nids, but a synthesized remedy finding's `clause` is the filed OBLIGATION\n-- for a `contradictory-clauses`/`self-referential` petition, the affected\ntask's own `successCriteria` verbatim, which a planner may write naming\nother task ids. Scanning it re-pointed the dependents of an unrelated\n`failed` task onto a remedy task that does not do its work: schedulable\nagain, reporting over work nobody will now do, and with no event to read\nit off, since only REJECTED edges emit.\n</code></pre>\n","status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":false,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[{"name":"event_loop_policy","time":{"start":1791980249757,"stop":1791980249757,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"tmp_path_factory","time":{"start":1791980249758,"stop":1791980249758,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"monkeypatch","time":{"start":1791980264653,"stop":1791980264653,"duration":0},"status":"passed","steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"hasContent":false,"attachmentStep":false},{"name":"_isolate_ambient_home_in_process","time":{"start":1791980264654,"stop":1791980264655,"duration":1},"s